  "mapping": {
    "authored_date": "2026-07-18",
    "deviation_notes": "The reserved-aura constant-chaos-DoT identity + zero-button uptime lands cleanly via aura geometry + drain ailment + PERSISTENCE_ENGINE_uptime + reservation economy. Minor drift: the item's signature 'chaos-damage-to-wearer-per-kill' self-harm loop (which forces the chaos-res investment that defines gearing) is expressed as a defensive-tax trait rather than a bespoke self-damage primitive; and the probe-attested 'wither' amp-debuff has no clean ailment lane. A player keeps the walk-and-melt feel; the self-damage-gearing-tension is generalized.",
    "grade": "CLOSE",
    "kit_id": "poe1-deaths-oath",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "ITEM-IS-THE-BUILD reserved-aura DoT: Death's Oath armour grants Death Aura, a persistent reserved aura dealing constant chaos DoT from the walking body (item_alterations dossier). Element chaos->shadow (§1); the constant life-decay DoT maps to DRAIN (§2), not poison (probe-facts guessed 'poison,wither' but the skill is a reserved-aura chaos-DoT field = drain lineage; poison is stacking-venom, which this is not). PERSISTENCE_ENGINE_uptime is the exact T4 door (zero-button always-on DoT uptime engine; RF/Death's-Aura archetype per §5 DoT/uptime ramps). CAPSTONE ABSTAINED (batch-03 100% guide-silent) — t4_door routed from core identity (reserved-aura constant-DoT = uptime engine) + probe economy fact (reserve model) per template fallback clause. WITHER NOTE: probe-facts lists 'wither' (a chaos-DoT-amp debuff stacking on enemies); no clean 16-ailment lane for wither-as-damage-amp (it is a taken-more-chaos-DoT stacking hex-adjacent effect) — nearest is curse:amplify but wither is self-applied-on-hit not a cast hex; recorded here, not minted (single instance). The item's self-damage-per-kill is a defensive tax expressed as chaos-resist investment, not an offensive mechanism. Era errata acknowledged (floor 1.x, verify_ledger authoritative).",
      "motion_frame": "zero-button aura-walker: equip the armour, walk into packs, chaos DoT clears at range with no active input (RF's chaos cousin)",
